---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import MarketingChrome from "../../components/MarketingChrome.astro";

const phoneDisplay = "(501) 413-3386";
const tel = "tel:+15014133386";
const sms = "sms:+15014133386";
---

<Base
  title="Dallas Bakery Websites, Free Demo by Text | NV Labs"
  description="Dallas bakeries: I build a free demo website for you remotely by phone and text. Menu, hours, and order requests. Call or text (501) 413-3386."
  image="/og.png"
  robots="index, follow"
>
  <MarketingChrome>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Dallas bakeries</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">Websites for Dallas bakeries, built remotely by phone and text</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Free demo first. Menu, hours, and order requests. Everything by call and text. No meeting
        needed.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-accent btn-lg" href={tel}>Call {phoneDisplay}</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={sms}>Text me</a>
        <a class="btn btn-text" href="/las-vegas-bakery-website/">Las Vegas bakery websites</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="remote-title">
      <h2 id="remote-title">Quick heads up: I work from Las Vegas</h2>
      <p>
        My name is Saad. I run NV Labs out of Las Vegas, and I work with Dallas bakeries by phone
        and text. You won't need to take a break from the ovens for a meeting. You text me some
        details and photos, I put together a demo, and I send you the link.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="dfw-title">
      <h2 id="dfw-title">DFW is a lot of ground to cover</h2>
      <p>
        A bakery in Bishop Arts pulls a different crowd than one in Plano. Someone in Deep Ellum
        after a show and a family in Richardson planning a birthday are looking for different
        things.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'll write your site around where you actually are and who you serve. Oak Cliff, Lakewood,
        Garland, Irving, wherever. It'll read like you talking about your neighborhood, not a list
        of city names.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="morning-title">
      <h2 id="morning-title">Kolaches, breakfast tacos, and the morning rush</h2>
      <p>
        Lots of Dallas bakeries do serious early morning business. If you sell kolaches, breakfast
        pastries, or coffee, I'll make the morning menu and opening time easy to spot. People
        grabbing something on the way to work don't want to scroll.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="orders-title">
      <h2 id="orders-title">Pre-orders for big days</h2>
      <p>
        Dozens of kolaches for the office, cookie boxes for the holidays, a wedding cake six months
        out. I'll set up order pages that fit what you sell, each with its own short form. One for
        party trays, one for celebration cakes, one for holiday pre-orders. You decide which ones
        you need.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="markets-title">
      <h2 id="markets-title">Farmers markets and pop-ups</h2>
      <p>
        If you sell at markets or pop-ups around town, I'll add a simple "Where to find us this
        week" section. Customers who love your stuff can track you down even on days the shop is
        closed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="how-title">
      <h2 id="how-title">How we'll work together</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Text me your bakery's name and what you bake.</li>
        <li>Send me your menu, hours, and some photos.</li>
        <li>I build your demo and text you the link.</li>
        <li>You tell me what to fix.</li>
        <li>If you like it, I put it live. If not, you're free to go.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <h2 id="faq-title">FAQ</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <div>
          <h3>How do you build a site for a Dallas bakery from Las Vegas?</h3>
          <p>
            Everything happens over text and phone. You send the details, I build, and you check the
            demo link from wherever you are. You don't have to be anywhere for it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Can you include the markets or pop-ups I sell at?</h3>
          <p>
            Yes. I'll add a schedule section you can update, or text me the new dates and I'll
            handle it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Do I need a big menu to make the site worth it?</h3>
          <p>
            No. A small menu, your hours, your address, and a few good photos make a solid site.
            Lots of great bakeries only do a handful of things.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="cta-title">
      <h2 id="cta-title">Let's build your Dallas bakery demo</h2>
      <p>Send me a text and we'll get going.</p>
      <a class="phone-big" href={tel}>{phoneDisplay}</a>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-accent btn-lg" href={tel}>Call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={sms}>Text</a>
      </div>
      <a class="back-home" href="/">Back to NV Labs home</a>
    </section>
  </MarketingChrome>
</Base>
